  "Sector rows are derived equal-weight composites of constituent stocks, not official NEPSE sub-indices; sector membership is today's map applied historically (survivorship caveat).",
  "Our taxonomy has 11 sectors: Trading companies are folded into Others, and mutual funds are an instrument type, not a sector index. The reference board this feature is modelled on carries 13 rows (Trading and Mutual Fund broken out) and different membership inside shared sectors, so levels differ while rankings track closely at short windows (rank correlation vs the reference's 2026-10-16 board: 0.99 at 7 days, 0.94 at 30, 0.90 at 90, 0.54 at 180, 0.86 at 365 \u2014 chained composites with different membership accumulate different long paths).",
